        "registryId": "NCT05579977",
        "overallStatus": "terminated",
        "sourceStatus": "Terminated"
      },
      "design": {
        "randomization": "Randomized",
        "masking": "Double-blind",
        "comparator": "Placebo and active comparator"
      },
      "population": "Adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on metformin and, separately, adults with obesity without type 2 diabetes mellitus.",
      "safetySummary": "The study was terminated early after elevated transaminases and unexpectedly high lotiglipron exposure were observed across this study and two Phase 1 DDI studies. In the obesity stratum, 81.5% had at least one treatment-emergent adverse event and 2.6% had at least one serious adverse event; gastrointestinal events were the most frequent.",
